            "ArialMT",
            "SymbolMT"
          ],
          "sizes": [
            11.04
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "Most vaccines are safe and effective to administer with no upper age limit and while timely",
          "bbox": [
            83.06,
            150.86,
            493.16,
            161.9
          ],
          "intersectsDrawing": true,
          "fonts": [
            "Calibri"
          ],
          "sizes": [
            11.04
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "vaccination should always be the aim, it is almost always better to vaccinate late than never.",
          "bbox": [
            83.06,
            165.62,
            504.69,
            176.66
          ],
          "intersectsDrawing": true,
          "fonts": [
            "Calibri",
            "Calibri-Bold"
          ],
          "sizes": [
            11.04
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "There are a small number of vaccines for which upper age limits do apply for administration3, but",
          "bbox": [
            83.06,
            179.48,
            519.32,
            191.42
          ],
          "intersectsDrawing": true,
          "fonts": [
            "Calibri"
          ],
          "sizes": [
            6.96,
            11.04
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "for most vaccine-preventable diseases (VPDs), providing vaccines late will still result in protection",
          "bbox": [
            83.06,
            195.14,
            520.17,
            206.18
          ],
          "intersectsDrawing": true,
          "fonts": [
            "Calibri"
          ],
          "sizes": [
            11.04
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "against morbidity and mortality.",
          "bbox": [
            83.06,
            209.9,
            231.99,
            220.94
          ],
          "intersectsDrawing": true,
          "fonts": [
            "Calibri",
